WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:02.300
People believing in each other

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.760
is the most wonderful
thing in the world!

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.930
So who ate my cake?

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.200
I told you, nobody ate it!

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.870
That's right. I wouldn't do that.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.940
I'd never do something so mean.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.110
Me, either.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.970
I don't really like
sweets to begin with.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.610
That's impossible!

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.110
The criminal is in this room!

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.500
You just said that people
who believe in each other

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.130
are important, didn't you?

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.790
Trust is only possible on
a foundation of proof!

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:40.090
No, isn't trust in the absence
of evidence the only real trust?

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.570
Sugisaki, platitudes won't
get you far in this world.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.800
I got lectured by a loli president.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.300
The criminal has to be in this room!

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.810
They just have to be!

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.750
You keep saying the
criminal is one of us,

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.900
but we're your friends.
Why doubt us?

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.410
Because the cake was here in
the student council room.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.410
Only the student council
members could've eaten it.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.600
But if one of left the door
unlocked after school,

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.160
anybody could've come in.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.790
The basis for your deductions
is pretty flimsy.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.020
A basis is supposed to be flimsy!

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.390
No, it's not.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.980
Anyway, calm down.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.100
I can't stay calm in this situation!

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.260
A man is dead!

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.600
No, he's not.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.000
Please don't make this
bigger than it is.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.140
You could call it the Cake Murder Case!

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.820
No, you can't.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.280
At best, it's theft.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:17.010
If it's already been eaten,
it's a Cannibalistic Cake Murder Case!

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:20.020
You're treating the cake
like a person, aren't you?

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.790
But you were going to eat it, right?

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.300
I'm allowed to eat it.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.290
It's mine, so I can do
whatever I want with it.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.040
I get the feeling you're
going to grow up to be

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.970
the worst mother in the world.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:38.470
Anyway, you're only treating this so lightly
because you're not the victims!

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.690
Help me find the criminal!

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.070
My calories depend on it!

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.270
It's hard to get motivated.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.960
All right. Sit down.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.670
Okay, tell me the details.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.220
All right, detective.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:58.490
I'm suddenly feeling very tired.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.070
Yes, we'll catch the culprit.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.360
Don't worry, miss.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.940
Tell us the details...

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:12.690
Um, I unlocked the door to
the student council room...

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.870
Kurimu-chan?

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.500
It's the lady from the school store.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.380
Here, this is for you.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:20.810
Here you go.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:27.390
This is to thank you for
all that you do for us.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.610
Really?

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:29.810
Thanks!

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.690
So you got the cake from the
lady from the school store.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.630
Was there anyone in the
student council room?

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.860
Nope.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.630
I'm the one who unlocked it.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:39.900
That's right.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:42.880
But why didn't you eat it right away?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.690
I wanted something to drink,
so I went to the vending machine.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.530
But when I came back...

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:55.180
It's gone! My cake is gone!

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.910
I see...

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.310
Which means...

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.030
The first person to arrive

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.730
while I was at
the vending machine...

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.580
They must've taken it!

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:08.320
By the time I got here,
Chizuru-san, Mafuyu-chan,

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.160
and Minatsu were here.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.160
But who was here first?

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.660
Me, probably.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.930
Nobody was here when I arrived.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.370
N-No!

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.020
My best friend was the culprit.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.020
I believed in you.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.800
Just so we're clear,
all I did was get here first.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.430
I didn't eat the cake.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.080
I didn't even know there was cake here.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.380
You're lying!

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.460
You're lying to me.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:34.560
Now, now...

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.960
But you couldn't miss a cake
sitting right on the desk.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:38.990
If it was there.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:40.190
But it wasn't.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.600
It wasn't?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.960
So the crime took place
before you arrived?

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.400
What's wrong?

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.150
I don't think the cake
was on the desk.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:51.940
Huh?

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:56.340
I put it on my chair when I
went to the vending machine.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.800
Why did you do that?

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.110
I hid it so nobody could
find it, obviously!

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.620
I see.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.920
So that's why she didn't see the cake.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:11.360
You can't trust her!

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:12.220
Um...

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.120
What?

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:19.300
Um, I'm reluctant to say this at
this point in the investigation...

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.530
Then butt out!

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:24.390
Chizuru was in the student
council room all by herself,

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.200
and that makes her the prime suspect!

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:30.540
No, I think Mafuyu was first...

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.540
Huh?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.810
I think I was first, too.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.050
Huh?

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.360
There was nobody here
when I arrived, either.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:41.130
I don't understand what you're saying.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.690
Explain!

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:48.650
So I was first, and Mafuyu was first,
and Chizuru-san was first, too.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.560
Objection!

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.830
That explanation doesn't make sense!

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:53.830
But it's true.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.750
She defeated me.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.570
N-No, she didn't!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.080
Mafuyu-chan, Minatsu. To be honest,
I don't understand, either.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.450
This isn't a sporting event for little kids,
so how could everyone come in first?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.070
I don't know what to tell you.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.450
There really wasn't anybody here.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:15.220
That's strange.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.040
I was spacing out here in
the student council room,

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.560
and then you came, Mafuyu-chan.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.110
What's going on here?

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:30.620
Oh, Akaba-senpai is talking about
the second time Mafuyu came.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.570
The second time?

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:32.800
Yes, the second.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:39.080
Nobody was here, so I decided
to go the restroom,

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.780
and then when I got back,
Akaba-senpai was here.

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.580
So that's it.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:49.330
Is that what happened
with you, too, Minatsu?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.320
Yeah, probably.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.520
When I arrived, nobody was here.

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:58.270
Then I remembered something I had to
do and went to the teacher's office...

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:02.090
...and when I got back,
Mafuyu and Chidzuru-san were here.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.230
And then I got here.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:05.780
Which means...

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:09.670
Anybody but Sugisaki could've done it!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.110
This is a pain.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:19.550
O-Okay, so let's be fair and
say all three of you did it!

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:20.770
Hold on one minute!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:21.750
Hey!

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.490
Magiru-sensei!

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:26.760
The most likely suspect!

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.510
Jeez.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.090
I'm the student council's advisor!

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.270
I return from confiscating books
that violate school rules,

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:41.550
and in my first scene in the new series,
you're treating me like a criminal!

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.790
So, what about the cake?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.780
Oh, I ate it.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:49.510
I knew it.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:53.140
And the cake wasn't enough, so now
you're eating that yakisoba bread.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.360
I'm only eating this because the woman

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.290
at the school store gave it to me.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:00.790
Come to think of it, the only
person who would do something

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.790
like this is Mahiru-sensei.

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:07.320
To just walk into the student council
room, see a cake, and eat it.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:10.800
That's exactly what
Magiru-sensei would do.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.810
She gets so little screen time I'd
completely forgotten to consider her!

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.680
I suppose I should've seen this coming.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.650
Don't flatter me so much,
it's embarrassing.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:20.550
I'm not flattering you!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.050
You don't have to get so mad just
because I ate Sakurano's cake!

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.820
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:30.320
I forgot the person I should've
suspected the most.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:32.560
My cake...

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.070
When I think about
Magiru-sensei eating it,

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:38.060
I feel sad instead of angry.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.610
Indeed.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.270
It's kind of our fault for
not being more careful.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.720
You guys are making too
big a deal out of this.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.500
I didn't eat the whole thing.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:47.250
Just a bite.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.110
Magiru-sensei, what did you say?

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:54.460
I said that when the students
are happy, I'm happy.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:56.510
You didn't say anything
close to that!

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.060
Live true to your dreams,
and have a brighter tomorrow!

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.170
You didn't say that, either!

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:04.050
Forget that! What about
the President's cake?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:08.500
Oh, how I stole Sakurano's
cake and gave it to you?

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:12.730
Key-kun?

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.320
Please don't lie like that!

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:19.460
Why are you turning me
into the prime suspect?

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:21.400
I thought it would be funny.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.680
Please stop.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:28.210
Anyway, is it true you only
ate a bite of the cake?

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.240
Yeah.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:33.300
I figured if I just had one bite,
even if she caught me, she'd forgive me.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.480
Which means...

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:40.430
The true culprit is someone else!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.480
You mean someone besides
me ate the cake?

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:45.430
Yes.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.430
It must've been them.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:52.660
Magiru-sensei, you know who ate it?

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:56.600
Yes, they came into the student
council room when I was leaving.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:01.330
Magiru-sensei!

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:02.720
What's wrong?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.890
I suddenly feel sick...

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.690
Sensei! Sensei!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:19.110
Misaki-sensei, what happened
to Magiru-sensei?

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.150
I can't say anything yet, but from
these symptoms it might be...

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:24.440
It might be...

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:27.830
No, I couldn't say yet.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:30.230
But don't touch that yakisoba bread.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:39.810
Magiru-sensei collapsed as she was
about to give us important evidence.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:41.590
Does that mean...

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:45.120
Misaki-sensei was acting odd, too.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.090
Could it be...

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.930
The true culprit poisoned her!

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.340
Poisoned...

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.460
We need to get that yakisoba bread now.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:54.900
I'll go.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.270
They say the criminal always returns
to the scene of the crime, don't they?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:04.040
We can't have our evidence
vanishing like your cake!

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:06.740
There it is.

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.800
Did the criminal really
return to the scene of the crime?

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.990
Here I am in the student council room!

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.690
Is something wrong, Lilicia-san?

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:22.630
And...

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.660
Hello, brother!

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.900
Eris-chan...

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:29.210
I'm sorry, but as you can
see, everybody's gone.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:31.580
We can't help you with your interviews.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:35.230
I heard something about
a "real culprit."

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:38.360
What are you talking about?

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.410
You can't fool me!

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:43.740
Who do you think I am?

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.650
I'm the head of the Newspaper
Club, Toudou Lilicia!

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:49.520
I know that. You don't
have to tell me.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:52.630
But what's Eris-chan doing here?

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:56.360
I'm babysitting my little sister,
Eris, at newspaper club today.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:59.870
And she demanded to come see you,
so I brought her. That's all.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.800
Are you doing well, brother?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.920
Yup, I sure am!

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.620
Have I gotten bigger, brother?

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.940
Maybe you're a little taller?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.940
What about my boobs?

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:15.510
No... I think you're a
little young for that.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:16.680
You're horrible.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.450
Then what do I say?

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:21.450
Am I cute?

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.190
Yes, very cute.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.860
Am I sexy?

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.460
Yes, very sexy!

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:28.190
Are you getting hot for Eris?

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.190
I sure am!

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:31.450
I'm calling the cops!

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.120
Crap.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.380
I wasn't really listening to her!

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:36.700
Why did I say I was
hot for a little kid?

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:41.130
Anyway, I think you've grown up.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.480
Now you're in love with me!

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:45.480
Sure am!

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:47.710
And hard down there!

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.480
Sure, super har—

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:50.670
Hello?

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:51.980
Is this the Department of Defense?

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:56.350
Could you at least call the cops
before you call the US Military?

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.750
Eris, this'll have a negative
impact on your education,

00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.990
so we're leaving.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.090
On her education?

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.200
There are a lot of things I
could say to that, but...

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.640
You should get back to
the newspaper club.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:07.680
No!

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.600
I want to stay with you!

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:13.500
It's not fair!
You made my body this way!

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.740
Ken Sugisaki, you...

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.800
No! I didn't do anything to Eris-chan!

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.230
You just lie there like a dead fish!

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:26.220
No, no! All she does is sit on
my lap and bounce around!

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.560
In my birthday suit!

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:31.620
I'll never forgive you, Sugisaki Ken!

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:32.660
No, no, no, no, no!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.180
That's a total a lie!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.260
Anyway, let's go home.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:41.590
Don't touch my little sister's breasts!

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:42.730
I-I didn't!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.800
You pervert! Pervert! Pervert!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.070
Stop it, sister!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:52.630
Are you okay, brother?

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.480
He's not moving!

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:56.540
No way!

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.790
It's okay.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.220
He's breathing.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.190
As long as they're breathing
and getting enough sunlight,

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.720
a human can live for 100 years.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.730
I learned something!

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:13.170
Anyway, we're getting out of here Eris.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:15.670
Bye, brother!

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:16.400
Come on.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:23.910
What's taking Key-kun so long?

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.910
Hey, Sugisaki's right there.

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:28.150
Huh?

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:30.420
He didn't get the yakisoba bread?

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:35.030
Who might you be?

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:36.940
Huh?

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:39.920
And who am I?

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.690
Stop playing around, Ken!

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:43.110
That's right, senpai.

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.160
Now's not the time.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.370
Not the time?

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.710
The cake theft, Key-kun!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:52.170
This "Key-kun" and "Ken"...
Is that me?

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:53.550
Of course it is!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.170
Stop screwing around.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:57.180
I'm not screwing around.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.940
I really don't know.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:00.450
Oh, I get it.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.910
Stop joking.

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:02.950
It's not funny.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.180
Aka-chan?

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:06.660
He's pretending to have
amnesia because he doesn't

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:08.840
want us to know he's the
one who took the cake!

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:09.930
Right?

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:14.160
Um, did I do something wrong?

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:16.310
I'm sorry.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:19.180
You really don't remember?

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.250
I don't.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.480
That's strange.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.470
Why did he suddenly lose his memories?

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:26.100
The real culprit!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:26.970
That's it!

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:31.640
They came to get the yakisoba
bread to hide the evidence.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.080
They <i>did</i> return to the
scene of the crime!

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.550
And he got into a fight with them.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.590
He got hit in a bad spot.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.900
Remember anything you can, Sugisaki!

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.490
Who did this to you?

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.220
I don't know...

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.320
The one thing I remember is...

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:48.730
The one thing you remember is...

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.500
Echo of Death.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.000
That's the one thing you remember?

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:55.730
Do you all know me?

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:59.030
You forgot that, too?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.170
I'm sorry.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:02.510
But I really don't remember anything.

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:03.920
Senpai...

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.750
The man who's always talking
about his harem is apologizing?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:10.210
Sugisaki's not Sugisaki!

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:11.870
Crying won't help.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.980
Let's all work together to
bring his memories back!

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:18.760
Yeah. He's the kind of simple
man who'd get amnesia easily.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.610
If we flip the switch,
he'll remember right away.

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.530
That's right...

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:24.690
Senpai.

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:28.530
Do you remember when I
told you I loved you?

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:31.310
Um...

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:34.270
And what did I say then?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:39.670
Actually, you were the one who
told me you loved me first.

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:42.280
Then are you and I lovers?

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:46.110
No. Personally, I think the
relationship between you

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:49.050
and Nakameguro-senpai is more important.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.790
A love triangle?

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:54.830
Or is this Nakameguro-san
my girlfriend?

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:57.630
Nakameguro-senpai is a guy!

00:17:58.630 --> 00:17:59.300
In other words...

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.280
That's right.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:03.300
Don't try to change his past!

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:08.910
You, too, Ken!

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:12.310
Don't act like a newborn chick and
believe everything you're told!

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.910
What was I like before
I lost my memories?

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:18.520
There are lots of stories about you!

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.820
I'm sure they're all horrible!

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.630
Th-That's not true.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.320
You did some good things.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.090
Like what?

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:28.670
Hmm...

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:29.830
Well...

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.070
Um...

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:33.900
They <i>are</i> all horrible, I knew it!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.840
No, there are just so
many, it's hard to pick!

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.560
It's all right.

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:42.160
I'm sure I'm just a total jerk!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.340
I think his memory might
be starting to come back!

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:45.960
One more push!

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:49.330
But I can't think of any other way
to bring back his memories...

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:53.340
Um... Maybe if he reads this!

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.580
Is this seriously me?

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:00.140
Did I talk about harems all the time?

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:03.290
I'm a lunatic.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:05.900
Ken... You don't have to
be so hard on yourself.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:09.270
I don't want to get any
more of my memories back.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:10.980
I've decided.

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:14.020
I'll abandon my past
and live a new life!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:17.600
This isn't my harem.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:18.560
That's all.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:21.890
You're the hero, you can't abandon
the entire series premise!

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:24.150
And that's the end of that.

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:26.470
Why does he look so innocent!

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.650
This isn't Sugisaki!

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:32.500
I think I can be an even
better person than I was!

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.720
Watch me.

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:37.160
I'll atone for the sins I committed
before I lost my memories.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:41.510
He's totally lost interest in
getting his memories back.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:44.440
It was a mistake to
show him those books.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.020
Why do you look so upset?

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:49.620
Well...

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.070
Seeing you like this makes me feel...

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:53.620
It's okay, Key-kun.

00:19:53.620 --> 00:19:56.410
There's no need for you to feel guilty.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:57.890
No.

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:02.190
I can't forgive myself
for making you sad.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:06.920
Those words are definitely
yours, Key-kun.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.430
They're enough for now.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.200
I'm sorry.

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.560
This is so strange.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.930
I made fun of Ken all the time,

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:19.050
but when I think about the
old him never coming back...

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:23.490
And so that's what happened.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:30.560
At least the student council
didn't eat the poisoned cake...

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.450
About that.

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.620
Magiru-sensei, you met the
woman from the school

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:38.070
store in front of the student
council room, right?

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.320
What about it?

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:44.260
There's a reason she went there.

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:48.270
It wasn't to give you the
bread that didn't sell.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.500
It was to take back the cake
she gave to Sakurano-san.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:56.510
That cake was way past
its expiration date.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.870
She saw somebody had taken a bite
from it and rushed to get rid of it.

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:05.150
Then the reason I collapsed
was food poisoning?

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:07.090
No, you just ate too much.

00:21:08.170 --> 00:21:10.590
But, Misaki-sensei, you said...

00:21:10.590 --> 00:21:14.890
I couldn't tell the students
you collapsed from overeating.

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:17.480
So the only thing I could
think of was to say

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.550
there was something
wrong with the bread.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:24.100
I'm sorry.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.550
That's okay, Key-kun.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:26.950
Just take it little by little.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:29.540
That's right. You're still Ken,
even without your memories.

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:34.590
The books Magiru-sensei
took were porn mags?

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:35.640
Let me see!

00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:39.520
This is great!

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.990
You like those naughty books, Sugisaki?

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.420
What are you saying, President?

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:47.800
I've always loved beautiful women.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.990
What is this place to you, Key-kun?

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:52.230
This is my harem.

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:54.190
What else could it be?

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:56.370
Are your memories back, Ken?

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.040
Oh. They were gone, weren't they?

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:03.390
I guess they all came back when
I saw how great this was.

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:07.650
After how sad we were...

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:10.380
All the work we did to try
and get your memories back...

00:22:10.380 --> 00:22:13.480
And they came back the instant
you saw a pornographic book?

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.320
Unforgivable.

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:19.390
Aww, you guys are exaggerating.

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:54.290
So in the end, who was the culprit?

00:23:54.290 --> 00:23:56.790
Who ate my cake?

00:23:56.790 --> 00:23:59.020
I think Ken's suspicious,
and there was no good reason

00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:01.660
to take him off the suspect
list from the start.

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:04.570
That's nonsense!

00:24:04.570 --> 00:24:07.300
Isn't it more likely that the President
is making the whole thing up?

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:10.800
There are some things it's
just not okay to say!

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:12.190
Argh! Who said

00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:15.310
"People believing in each other is
the most wonderful thing in the world!"

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:20.170
I've never found the
President's words

00:24:20.170 --> 00:24:22.310
as relevant as they were this time.

00:24:25.530 --> 00:24:26.990
What do you want for breakfast?

00:24:26.990 --> 00:24:28.160
I'll go fish up some tuna!

00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:28.850
Elaborate!

00:24:28.850 --> 00:24:30.850
Can we have cake for breakfast?

00:24:30.850 --> 00:24:31.990
If it's less than 300 yen.

00:24:31.990 --> 00:24:33.640
I'll take coffee at dawn.

00:24:33.640 --> 00:24:35.650
The Student Council eats breakfast!

00:24:35.650 --> 00:24:36.830
This time it's breakfast!

00:24:36.830 --> 00:24:39.020
It's "The Student Council Looks For Work!"
